<h1>Privacy Policy for BibelWallpaper</h1>
<p><em>Effective date: September 25, 2026</em></p>

<h2>Who we are</h2>
<p>BibelWallpaper is an Android app that shows Bible verses as wallpaper on the lock screen and/or home screen of your device and changes them automatically.</p>

<h2>Summary</h2>
<p>BibelWallpaper does not collect any personal data, and the developer never receives any data from the app. The app:</p>
<ul>
  <li>has no internet connection (it does not hold the network access permission);</li>
  <li>uses no analytics, tracking, or advertising SDKs;</li>
  <li>requires no account or sign-in;</li>
  <li>has no servers of its own and never sends information to third parties.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Data stored on your device</h2>
<p>The app stores the following only on your device, in its private storage:</p>
<ul>
  <li>your settings (language, font, colors, background, update mode and similar);</li>
  <li>the history of recently shown verses and your favorite verses;</li>
  <li>a copy of the background photo you chose (see "Photo access").</li>
</ul>
<p>Uninstalling the app deletes all of this data.</p>

<h2>Android backup</h2>
<p>If backup to your Google account is turned on in your phone's settings, Android may include the app's settings, verse history and favorites in your personal device backup, so they can be restored after reinstalling the app or on a new phone. This backup is created and stored by Android and Google in your own Google account; the developer has no access to it. The copy of your background photo is excluded from this cloud backup. You can turn backup off at any time in your phone's settings.</p>

<h2>Photo access</h2>
<p>If you choose a background image, the app uses Android's built-in photo picker. Through it, the app gets access only to the single image you selected, not to your gallery. The app saves a resized copy of that image in its private storage, so your wallpaper keeps working even if the original photo is deleted. The copy is used only to draw your wallpaper, is replaced when you choose another photo, is not included in cloud backups and never leaves your phone through the app.</p>

<h2>Sharing verses</h2>
<p>When you use "Share", the verse is passed as text or as an image to the app you choose (for example, a messenger). To share an image, the app creates it temporarily in its own cache. Nothing is shared unless you do it yourself.</p>

<h2>Bug reports</h2>
<p>If you tap "Report a bug", your own email app opens with a prepared message that contains the app version, the Android version and the phone model. Nothing is sent unless you send the email yourself. Emails received this way are used only to reply to you and to fix problems.</p>

<h2>Home screen widgets</h2>
<p>The widgets show verses from the app's built-in collection and work on the same principles: no data leaves your device.</p>

<h2>Permissions</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Set wallpaper</strong> - to place the verse on your lock screen and/or home screen.</li>
  <li><strong>Notifications</strong> - to show the notification that Android requires while the app changes the verse in the background.</li>
  <li><strong>Background service and battery optimization exemption</strong> - so that the verse can change every time you turn off the screen, even when the app is closed.</li>
  <li><strong>Start after reboot</strong> - to resume automatic verse changes after the phone restarts.</li>
</ul>
<p>None of these permissions is used to access personal data.</p>

<h2>Children</h2>
<p>The app does not collect data from anyone, including children, and is suitable for all ages.</p>

<h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
<p>If this privacy policy changes, an updated version will be posted on this page with a new effective date.</p>

